  "pos": "n.",
  "meaningEn": "1. Kool Aid popsicles hawked by street vendors, especially near Waterside bus depot in Monrovia; so called because popsicles were shaped like breasts in conformity to the corners of the plastic baggies in which they were frozen. 2. Platform shoes or shoes with extremely high heels; derived from photo of Prince Nicko on the cover of his album titled “Sweet Mother.” [Arose in the 1970s, when “Sweet Mother” by Prince Nicko and the Rocafi Jazz Band enjoyed widespread popularity.]",
